course: dictionary
lesson: 13282
title: Gracious: kind, polite and elegant
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Gracious has several meanings, and the context tells you which one fits. A gracious person is kind and polite, especially to people who have less power than they do. «The gracious queen smiled at every child who bowed to her.» The queen is kind and polite to the children, so gracious means kind here.
explain: «She was gracious in defeat, shaking the winner's hand and saying well done.» Gracious in defeat means losing and still being polite and fair. Gracious can also describe a way of living that is comfortable and elegant, as in «gracious living».
explain: Look for «gracious!» said on its own. «Gracious! I didn't know you were coming.» Goodness gracious! is an old-fashioned way to show surprise. In church, gracious describes God as full of mercy and kindness.
fact: Gracious means kind, polite and generous, especially to people who have less power.
fact: «Gracious» can also mean graceful and elegant, as in «gracious living».
fact: «Gracious!» or «Goodness gracious!» is an old-fashioned way to show surprise.
fact: «Gracious in defeat» means being polite and fair when you lose.
fact: In church, gracious describes God as full of mercy and kindness.
exercise: «The gracious host made sure every guest had a warm drink.» What does gracious mean here? | Very tired | Angry and loud | Hungry for cake | *Kind and polite
exercise: «Goodness gracious! Look at the size of that cake!» What is gracious showing? | Anger | Tiredness | Sadness | *Surprise
exercise: «She was gracious in defeat, shaking the winner's hand.» What does gracious in defeat mean? | Crying loudly after a loss | Winning every game | *Polite and fair when losing | Refusing to play again
test: «The gracious lady invited the poor children to her garden party.» What does gracious mean here? | Cross and loud | Very small | *Kind and generous | Lost in the garden
test: Ben says gracious only means «thank you». Why is he wrong? | It means angry | It only means thank you | *It has several meanings, and context decides which one | It is a number
exam: «The gracious house had soft carpets, tall windows and beautiful gardens.» What does gracious mean here? | Hungry | Rude and noisy | *Elegant and comfortable | Wet and grey
